WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.457 --> 00:00:16.199
only one thing left to do, now," said Tom.

2
00:00:16.219 --> 00:00:21.284
"We have to send the family a mysterious warning, like they do in books."

3
00:00:22.425 --> 00:00:26.128
So that same night, we pushed a note under the front door to the house.

4
00:00:27.229 --> 00:00:28.790
It read: BEWARE.

5
00:00:29.271 --> 00:00:30.152
Trouble is coming.

6
00:00:30.892 --> 00:00:33.995
Someone is going to try to steal the escaped slave.

7
00:00:34.495 --> 00:00:35.716
From your unknown friend.

8
00:00:38.258 --> 00:00:41.201
The next night, we drew a coffin on the back door.

9
00:00:42.161 --> 00:00:44.183
By now the Phelpses were very nervous.

10
00:00:45.164 --> 00:00:50.208
They jumped at every noise, and if anything brushed against them, they thought it was a snake.

11
00:00:51.209 --> 00:00:53.571
They asked some neighbors to help them guard their house.

12
00:00:55.172 --> 00:01:00.016
That evening, there were 15 farmers, armed with guns, sitting in the parlor.

13
00:01:00.976 --> 00:01:04.138
Some of the men said they were going to go down to the shed and guard it.

14
00:01:05.259 --> 00:01:08.641
That's when I knew that Tom had gone too far with his crazy plan.

15
00:01:09.742 --> 00:01:11.604
We should have freed Jim days ago.

16
00:01:12.244 --> 00:01:14.345
In a panic, Tom and I ran to the hut.

17
00:01:16.107 --> 00:01:20.250
We went through our tunnel to Jim's shed and told him we had to escape right away.

18
00:01:21.370 --> 00:01:25.093
Suddenly, we heard men outside the door, putting the key in the lock.

19
00:01:26.054 --> 00:01:29.216
Just as they pushed the door open, we hurried into the tunnel.

20
00:01:30.208 --> 00:01:33.229
The men didn't see the hole because it was under Jim's bed.

21
00:01:35.069 --> 00:01:38.690
In the dark, we crept out of the hut and ran across the yard.

22
00:01:39.551 --> 00:01:43.752
Jim and I got over the fence, but Tom's pants caught on a splinter of wood.

23
00:01:44.772 --> 00:01:48.173
The splinter broke off with a loud snap and Tom was free.

24
00:01:49.093 --> 00:01:51.194
But one of the men yelled, "Who's there?

25
00:01:51.634 --> 00:01:52.855
Stop, or I'll shoot!"

26
00:01:54.595 --> 00:01:57.656
Bullets whizzed over our heads as we ran through the woods.

27
00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:02.243
We hid behind some bushes until the men gave up looking for us.

28
00:02:03.363 --> 00:02:07.887
Then we scrambled down the riverbank, untied the raft, and got onboard.

29
00:02:08.987 --> 00:02:13.411
We headed for the middle of the river, to a small island called Spanish Island.

30
00:02:13.431 --> 00:02:18.094
"Well, Jim," I said, "you are a free man.

31
00:02:18.574 --> 00:02:20.376
I hope you won't ever be a slave again."

32
00:02:21.737 --> 00:02:26.280
We were both happy for a minute, until we saw that Tom had been shot in the leg!

33
00:02:27.364 --> 00:02:29.545
Jim and I helped him into the hut on the raft.

34
00:02:30.606 --> 00:02:34.008
We bandaged Tom's bleeding calf with one of the duke's old shirts.

35
00:02:35.449 --> 00:02:37.770
Then we looked at each other with serious faces.

36
00:02:38.710 --> 00:02:42.132
Jim said, "Huck, we have to get a doctor for Tom.

37
00:02:42.833 --> 00:02:45.214
Even if it means that I am captured again."

38
00:02:46.294 --> 00:02:47.335
I knew Jim was right.

39
00:02:48.355 --> 00:02:51.517
I paddled back to the shore in the canoe that we kept on the raft.

40
00:02:52.498 --> 00:02:53.938
Jim and Tom stayed behind.

41
00:02:54.879 --> 00:02:56.540
The town doctor was a kind man.

42
00:02:57.564 --> 00:03:01.787
Even though I woke him up late at night, he dressed and came with me right away.

43
00:03:02.968 --> 00:03:07.011
I made up a story that my brother Sid and I had been hunting on the island.

44
00:03:08.292 --> 00:03:10.713
There had been an accident with Sid's gun, I said.

45
00:03:11.714 --> 00:03:16.277
When the doctor saw the old canoe, however, he didn't think it was safe for two people.

46
00:03:17.538 --> 00:03:20.240
He said that he would paddle over to the raft by himself.

47
00:03:22.662 --> 00:03:25.884
I waited for a long time, but the doctor didn't come back.

48
00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:28.942
I was worried about Tom's wound.

49
00:03:31.043 --> 00:03:35.046
Then I realized that it was morning; I had fallen asleep on the riverbank.

50
00:03:36.207 --> 00:03:39.730
I went to the doctor's house and learned that he still hadn't come back.

51
00:03:41.371 --> 00:03:45.534
I decided that I had to find out how Tom was, even if I had to swim to

52
00:03:45.574 --> 00:03:46.054
the island.

53
00:03:47.275 --> 00:03:50.658
But as I was hurrying down the street, I met Uncle Silas.

54
00:03:50.678 --> 00:03:52.379
"Why, Tom!"

55
00:03:52.859 --> 00:03:53.480
he exclaimed.

56
00:03:54.464 --> 00:03:57.166
"Your aunt and I have been so worried about you and Sid.

57
00:03:57.666 --> 00:03:58.706
Where have you been all night?"

58
00:04:00.567 --> 00:04:02.468
Once again, I made up a story.

59
00:04:03.449 --> 00:04:08.492
I told Uncle Silas that Sid and I had run to help the men chase the runaway slave.

60
00:04:09.532 --> 00:04:11.173
But we lost them in the dark woods.

61
00:04:12.094 --> 00:04:14.595
We were so tired that we fell asleep there.

62
00:04:15.956 --> 00:04:19.257
I said that Sid had gone to buy rolls for our breakfast from the bakery.

63
00:04:20.138 --> 00:04:23.760
As soon as Sid came back, we were planning to go home to Aunt Sally.

64
00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:27.921
Uncle Silas said we must go to the bakery to get Sid.

65
00:04:31.103 --> 00:04:32.483
But of course he wasn't there.

66
00:04:33.544 --> 00:04:38.926
Finally, Uncle Silas said that we shouldn't wait any longer to get me home, where Aunt Sally was

67
00:04:38.986 --> 00:04:39.887
waiting anxiously.

68
00:04:40.927 --> 00:04:42.748
Then he would go out to search for Sid.

69
00:04:44.489 --> 00:04:47.570
Aunt Sally was so happy to see me that she cried and hugged me.

70
00:04:51.924 --> 00:04:56.247
She was very upset that Sid wasn't with us, but I told the same story again.

71
00:04:57.288 --> 00:04:59.109
Uncle Silas went out again to search.

72
00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:01.351
The hours went by.

73
00:05:01.891 --> 00:05:04.713
Aunt Sally was worried because her nephew was lost.

74
00:05:05.914 --> 00:05:09.016
I knew he wasn't lost, but I was afraid he was dying.

75
00:05:10.137 --> 00:05:15.120
I couldn't tell anyone, though, because if they found Tom, they would find Jim and make him a

76
00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:15.761
slave again.

77
00:05:17.602 --> 00:05:19.984
By dinnertime, Uncle Silas hadn't returned.

78
00:05:20.900 --> 00:05:23.062
By bedtime, he still wasn't back.

79
00:05:23.783 --> 00:05:25.345
I went up to my room and cried.

80
00:05:26.386 --> 00:05:28.248
Later Aunt Sally stopped by my room.

81
00:05:28.268 --> 00:05:35.114
"I know how worried you are," she said, "but I want you to promise that you won't sneak

82
00:05:35.195 --> 00:05:36.256
out to look for Sid."

83
00:05:37.577 --> 00:05:40.380
She was a good, kind person, so I promised.
